const e={tempoAndCardAdvantage:{description:"Tempo describes how efficiently you're using resources vs opponent. Card advantage measures cards in hand relative to opponent.",keyPoints:["Early deployment: Summon low-cost characters that challenge effectively","Removal timing: Use removal before opponent's synergy triggers","Quest/Challenge balance: Know when to exert for lore vs staying ready","Combining tempo + card advantage is lethal - control the flow of the game"],tempoDecks:"Feature 2-3 cost creatures with immediate board impact, snowball advantage by having more creatures than opponent"},inkCurve:{description:"Balanced distribution of cards across different costs for playable options at every stage",recommended:{lowCost:"8-10 cards at 1-2 cost (early pressure)",midCost:"10-12 cards at 3-4 cost (board building)",highCost:"8-10 cards at 5-6 cost (value generators)",bombs:"2-4 cards at 7+ cost (finishers)"},warning:"Don't get stuck with high-cost uninkable cards - consider 40-50% of deck should be ink-eligible"},keywordSynergy:{evasive:"Can only be challenged by other Evasive characters. Deck built around Evasive forces opponent to run Evasive or use removal",bodyguard:"Can redirect challenges, protecting key questers. Don't waste them as ink",shift:"Play upgraded versions at reduced cost if base version exists. Accelerates tempo significantly",importance:"Don't neglect staple effects just to jam more synergy"},metaAnalysis:{steps:["Identify common decks in your area/online","Spot their weaknesses","Reserve 2-3 flex slots for meta tech cards","If sideboarding allowed, treat as targeted solution kit"]}},a={mulliganStrategy:{goal:"Assemble an ink curve with 1-drop on turn 1, 2-drop on turn 2, etc",aggressive:"Mulligan duplicate ink costs, keeping best of each drop",examples:["Two 1-drops, three 3-drops = keep one 1-drop and one 3-drop, bottom rest to find 2-drop and 4-drop","Perfect 1-2-3-4 curve + 4 different 4-drops = keep good 4-drop, bottom others to find 5-6 drop"],warning:"Be careful with non-inkable cards - bottom some if hand has more than 2. Avoid aggressive mulligans if deck has 25%+ non-inkable"},inkellingDecisions:{goal:"Plan ahead, mapping first few turns to ensure smooth curve",principles:["Turn 1-5: Always ink something to curve out properly","Ink the worst card you won't play if something better is available","If hand is worst 4-drop, best 5-drop, two 2-drops: ink worst 4-drop and keep excess 2-drop","Late game: Stop inking after turn 5-6 if you've hit natural mana cap (e.g., 5 ink spent/turn)"]},questingVsChallenging:{principle:"Only quest when ahead and/or safe. Game is about maintaining board state that gains 20 lore faster.",rules:["If opponent is ahead in race: challenge defensively","If board is equal: don't quest if it gives favorable trade","Board control is more important than rushing lore early game","Challenge is control strategy, questing is aggro strategy"]},cardValuation:{overperformers:["Efficient removal spells","Ramp spells","Evasive characters","Bodyguards","Card advantage generators"],note:"Willpower appears more important than strength or lore values"}},t={whoIsTheBeatdown:{description:"Fundamental question: Am I trying to finish fast (beatdown) or stabilize and grind (control)?",beatdown:"Player trying to push to win as fast as possible. Quest aggressively. Finish before opponent's finishers matter.",control:"Player stabilizing and stopping opponent. Challenge and remove threats. Buy time for your answers.",fluid:"In Lorcana the question changes turn by turn based on board state and hand strength",decisionRule:"When tempted to quest for lore: Am I the beatdown? If no, prioritize stabilizing over questing"},tempoPlays:{definition:"Plays that build momentum or disrupt opponent's progress while advancing your own",example:"Bounce high-cost threat back to hand instead of removing. Costs them another turn, gives you time to draw answer",value:"Buying one turn of unopposed questing (if you're beatdown) is regularly enough to win games",principle:"Lorcana is game of small incremental advantages that add up to 20 lore"},stayOnCurve:{definition:"Every turn drop card into inkwell and play card using that ink. 1-drop T1, 2-drop T2, etc",mistake:"Playing inkable 1-costs on turn 2 just because you have ink available",priority:"Ensure you can drop that amazing 6-8 cost card on turn 6-8 when you hit it",overInking:"Don't keep going past natural mana cap. Most decks lack drawing power. Holding cards lets you play around removal"},playAroundRemoval:{ruby:"Be aware of: Be Prepared (board wipe at 7 ink), Dragon Fire (4 copies likely)",steel:"Be aware of: Grab Your Sword, Smash, Fire the Cannons (assume 3-4 copies if seen)",tactics:["Don't throw down weak characters to get exiled","Play smaller threat first to bait removal before deploying your big threat","Keep characters in hand to replace removed ones","Don't overcommit to board vs Ruby/Steel"]},tradeUp:{definition:"Exchange a card for opponent's card of higher value (usually by ink cost)",good:"Your 1-cost takes out their 2-cost - you're ahead",bad:"Your 4-cost trades with their 3-cost - net negative",principle:"Equal trades only work if you're ahead. Always trade upwards in value"},patience:{principle:"Lorcana is won by building and maintaining board state that reaches 20 lore, not racing",timing:"Only throw everything on board when opponent is 15+ lore AND board shows you'll lose in 2 turns",rules:["Only quest aggressively if you're beatdown","Disrupt opponent's tempo where possible","Play ink and cards on curve","Don't get baited into board wipes","Trade to remove higher value opponent cards","Keep your cool"]}},r={rubyAmethystAggroControl:{idea:"Ruby aggressive minions + Amethyst draw and Shift for sustained pressure",cards:["Low-cost Ruby characters with 2 lore icons for quick questing","Amethyst Shift characters that upgrade cheaply to outscale","Removal songs/actions that double as ink if ahead or removal if behind"],decisions:["When to quest aggressively vs save for challenges","Timing Shift upgrades without losing tempo","Balancing uninkable vs inkable card ratio"]},emeraldSapphireMidrangeControl:{idea:"Sturdy Sapphire characters for stalling, mid-cost Emerald units that debuff and control",curve:{early:"1-2 cost defensive minions or item draw",mid:"3-5 cost creatures that remove or hamper threats",late:"6-7 cost bombs that flip board or collect lore"},strengths:["Grinding out value-based decks by outlasting","Surviving hyper-aggro with midrange taunts and removal","Playing defense until big finishers online"]},princessSynergy:{idea:"Leverage synergy cards that buff Princess characters specifically",considerations:["Enough synergy cards for consistent triggers (don't spread too thin)","Deck functions if key synergy pieces are banished","Include Bodyguard or Evasive support","Don't neglect universal removal options"]}},n={aggro:{goal:"Win by turn 5-6 with early pressure",mulligan:"Aggressively mulligan for low-cost openers, accept weak late game",strategy:"Snowball advantage with efficient creatures, force opponent into defensive plays",curveAdjustment:"If avg cost >4, replace 5-8 high-cost cards with low-cost units (1-3)",questions:["Do I have enough 1-3 cost creatures for early pressure?","Can I threaten lethal by turn 6?","Do I have evasive creatures to force unfavorable blocks?"]},control:{goal:"Survive until turn 7+, win with locked board",mulligan:"Search for removal and card draw, accept weak early game",strategy:"Answer every threat, stabilize board, deploy finishers once safe",curveAdjustment:"If avg cost <4, add 4-6 high-cost cards (5+) as finishers",questions:["Do I have enough removal for major threats?","Do I have card draw to maintain tempo?","Can I stabilize before opponent's threats dominate?"]},midrange:{goal:"Tempo and value, win with efficient threats into turn 7",mulligan:"Balance of threats and answers, aim for perfect curve",strategy:"Value trades, efficient board presence, flexible answers",curveAdjustment:"If avg cost 4-4.5 (ideal), keep curve. <4: add mid-costers. >4.5: add low-costers",questions:["Do I have 50% threats and 50% answers?","Can I make trades favorably?","Is my deck consistent turn to turn?"]}},o={recommended:"High-cost inkable characters are like MTG's land/bomb split cards - Lorcana allows top-heavy curves",upgrade:"Remove low-impact items/actions, add more 5-7 cost characters",underperformers:["Dinglehopper","Part of Your World","Hakuna Matata","Stampede","Steal from the Rich","He's Got a Sword","Ransack","Magic Golden Flower","Frying Pan"]},s={deck_construction_checklist:["✓ 60 cards exactly","✓ Max 4 copies per card (except special)","✓ 2 colors maximum for constructed","✓ 8-10 one-drops for early pressure","✓ 40-50% of deck is ink-eligible","✓ Balanced curve from turns 1-7+","✓ Includes removal (3-6 removal spells)","✓ Includes card draw (2-4 draw effects)","✓ Clear win condition"],early_game_priorities:["Mulligan aggressively for curve","Land your first creature turn 1-2","Maintain board presence (1+ creature)","Watch opponent's opening plays","Play to ink curve (T1-T5 add ink each turn)"],mid_game_priorities:["Balance tempo vs card advantage","Make favorable trades (1-cost for 2-cost)","Hold removal for key threats","Build towards your finishers","Watch opponent's hand size"],late_game_priorities:["Protect your lore total (20 is finish line)","Control board state completely","Deploy finishers when safe","Have outs if opponent has threats","Close out cleanly"],critical_decision_moments:{do_I_quest_or_challenge:"Ask: Am I the beatdown? If yes, quest. If no, challenge.",which_cards_to_ink:"Ink worst cards you won't play. Plan first 5-6 turns ahead.",when_to_hold_removal:"Keep removal for game-ending threats, not low-impact creatures.",how_many_creatures:"Minimum 1-2 creatures per turn early, 3+ mid-game, control board late.",when_do_i_pass:"Only pass when board is safe or you're out of playable cards."},deckbuilding_archetypes:{tempo_aggro:{goal:"Win turns 5-6 with early pressure",cards:"12-15 one-drops, 10-12 two-drops, 8-10 three-drops, 3-4 finishers",removal:"Efficient 2-3 cost removal, burn/direct damage",draw:"1-2 card draw effects (optional, tempo is more important)"},midrange:{goal:"Win turns 6-7 with efficient threats + answers",cards:"6-8 one-drops, 8-10 two-drops, 10-12 three-cost, 8-10 four-cost, 4-6 five-plus",removal:"4-6 removal spells, flexible answers",draw:"2-4 card draw effects for consistency"},control:{goal:"Win turn 8+ after locking board",cards:"2-4 one-drops, 4-6 two-drops, 8-10 three-cost, 8-10 four-cost, 6-8 five-plus",removal:"8-10 removal spells, board wipes, sweepers",draw:"4-6 card draw effects for consistency"}},common_mistakes_to_avoid:["Playing ink candidates early when you should save them","Questing when you should challenge (behind in tempo)","Overcommitting creatures to board with removal coming","Keeping too many singletons (reduces consistency)","Not counting opponent's lore (always know the race)","Forgetting to ask: Who is the beatdown?","Mulliganing too conservatively for perfect curve","Inking cards you might need later (plan ahead!)","Not playing around known removal threats","Wasting removal on low-impact creatures"],card_valuation_guide:{overrated:["High-cost creatures without synergy (6+ costs)","Cards that only work in specific situations","Singleton copies of mediocre cards","Cards that can't be inked (except essential)"],underrated:["One-drops (early pressure matters!)","Removal spells (tempo + card advantage)","Evasive creatures (force removal or favorable blocks)","Cheap card draw (consistency wins games)","Bodyguards (protect your threats)"]},matchup_framework:{vs_aggro:{priority:"Survival → Board control → Reach 20 lore",tactics:"Challenge everything, remove threats immediately, life gain if available",win_condition:"Out-value their threats with efficient removal + stabilization"},vs_midrange:{priority:"Tempo → Favorable trades → Out-value them",tactics:"Trade up (your 1-drop for their 2-drop), keep hand full, pressure lore",win_condition:"Accumulate small advantages into large leads"},vs_control:{priority:"Consistency → Board presence → Overwhelm answers",tactics:"Hold cards in hand, bait removal with small threats, deploy finishers when answers are gone",win_condition:"Have 1-2 finishers when they're out of removal"}}},i={resource_management:{ink_management:"Plan first 6 turns of inking. Don't over-ink past natural mana cap. Reserve ink for curve plays.",hand_management:"Hold cards to play around removal. Don't empty hand on single turn unless you're beatdown.",threat_management:"Identify 2-3 key threats per turn. Know what you can remove. Know what threatens you."},game_theory:{information_advantage:"Watch opponent's hand size. Count their discard. Predict their plays.",decision_trees:"Each action has pros/cons. Consider opponent's responses. Play defensively if unsure.",positioning:"Order of play matters. Play threats after removal bait. Chain advantages."},tournament_preparation:{meta_awareness:"Research top decks in your area. Know their gameplans. Build counters.",sideboarding:"If allowed, prepare answers to meta decks. 8-15 flex cards.",mental_game:"Stay calm. Play at consistent pace. Don't tilt after losses."},rapid_improvement:{playtesting:"Play 20+ games with your deck before tournament",notes:"Write down what beat you and why. Adjust accordingly.",watching_vods:"Study pro players' decision-making. Learn from their mistakes.",deck_refinement:"Cut cards that never help. Add cards you desperately needed."},meta_predictions:{watch_for:"If one deck wins multiple events, expect it everywhere",build_counters:"If Evasive is dominant, add cheap removal or Evasive of your own",stay_flexible:"Keep 2-3 flex slots for last-minute tech cards"}},l={dominantArchetypes:{rubyAmethyst:{archetype:"Emerald/Sapphire Control",description:"Current DLC benchmark deck. Ink acceleration plus card flow into high-impact finishers.",strengths:["Excellent card advantage loops","Strong inevitability in longer games","Flexible answers across multiple matchups","Reliable post-Winterspell conversion rate"],weaknesses:["Can stumble under very fast openers","Requires disciplined mulligans to avoid slow hands","Targeted hand disruption can delay setup"],howToCounter:["Pressure hard on turns 1-3 before acceleration engines stick","Force awkward defensive lines with evasive or challenger threats","Hold premium interaction for Clarabelle/Basil turns","Avoid overextending into swing turns; keep reload in hand"]},sapphireSteel:{archetype:"Ruby/Steel Winterspell Tempo",description:"Winterspell-era tempo deck that converts efficient 2-4 drops into consistent pressure and favorable trades.",strengths:["Strong curve pressure with flexible interaction","Excellent at punishing slow starts","Efficient challenge math in mid-game turns","Winterspell cards add tempo-positive utility"],weaknesses:["Can run out of gas if first wave is answered","Less favored into heavy removal control mirrors","Needs proactive sequencing to maintain momentum"],howToCounter:["Use resilient blockers and removal to blunt early curve","Force value trades that break tempo chains","Stabilize around turns 4-5 and pivot to card advantage","Prioritize answers to Winterspell tempo payoffs"]},emeraldSapphire:{archetype:"Amethyst/Sapphire Value",description:"Card flow and acceleration shell that goes over creature mirrors while maintaining interaction density.",strengths:["High consistency through draw and filtering","Strong late-game inevitability","Good matchup into fair midrange decks","Flexible threat-answer balance"],weaknesses:["Can be pressured by hyper-aggro openings","Requires careful resource planning","Vulnerable to concentrated hand disruption"],howToCounter:["Apply early pressure before draw engines turn on","Attack ink acceleration pieces when possible","Sequence threats to tax answers over multiple turns","Leverage haste/tempo windows to close before inevitability"]},amberSteel:{archetype:"Amber/Emerald Dogs",description:"Fast proactive aggro line that keeps punishing greedy setups in DLC-level play.",strengths:["Explosive early board presence","Strong conversion of cheap bodies into lore pressure","Punishes slow mulligans and clunky curves","Maintains threat density with low-cost synergy pieces"],weaknesses:["Can lose to concentrated board wipes","Lower top-end staying power in drawn-out games","Requires tight sequencing to maximize damage"],howToCounter:["Prioritize cheap removal and efficient blockers","Force low-value trades early to reduce snowball potential","Stabilize life/lore race before committing finishers","Keep one reset option for their widest board turns"]}},inkColorMetaRoles:{ruby:{role:"Aggressive Tempo",description:"Rush and Evasive abilities enable early pressure",metaPosition:"Staple in aggro and tempo decks. Strong against control.",currentTrend:"Rising in popularity post-Fabled, especially in Ruby/Steel variants"},sapphire:{role:"Card Draw & Control",description:"Ink management and resource generation enable consistent play",metaPosition:"Essential for control decks. Strong in midrange.",currentTrend:"Dominant in Sapphire/Steel control, which is tier-1"},emerald:{role:"Gameplay Manipulation",description:"Creature control and game-state effects",metaPosition:"Strong in midrange. Versatile in hybrid decks.",currentTrend:"Consistent performer in Emerald/Sapphire midrange"},steel:{role:"Defensive Power",description:"High-power creatures with Resist abilities",metaPosition:"Increasingly important in control and tempo-control decks",currentTrend:"Rising popularity in Sapphire/Steel and Ruby/Steel"},amber:{role:"Defense & Recovery",description:"Healing and stabilization effects",metaPosition:"Strong in defensive decks. Emerging in tempo-control.",currentTrend:"Solid performer in Amber/Steel defensive decks"},amethyst:{role:"Hand Manipulation",description:"Discard pressure and spell-based control",metaPosition:"Staple in aggro-control. Critical for hand denial.",currentTrend:"Essential in Ruby/Amethyst, highest performer currently"}},metaTechGuide:{against_rubyAmethyst:["Resist creatures - Steel blockers don't take damage from Rush","Early board wipes - prevent snowballing in turns 1-3","Healing/Recovery - Amber effects stabilize before they finish","Card draw engines - rebuild after hand disruption","Creatures with evasion blockers - trade efficiently"],against_sapphireSteel:["Turn 1-2 pressure - force answers before draw engine","Hand disruption - prevent them from drawing key answers","Multiple simultaneous threats - overwhelm removal suite","Evasive creatures - bypass their Steel blockers","Fast clock - win before they stabilize board"],against_emeraldSapphire:["Redundant threats - they can't answer everything","Resource denial - discard their answers before turn plays","Cheap efficient creatures - establish presence while they setup","Removal immune creatures - forces their answers to be inefficient","Tempo pressure - apply damage faster than they can stabilize"],against_amberSteel:["Aggressive early turns - don't let them stabilize","Hand disruption - prevent recovery setup","Multiple threats - force inefficient trades","Evasion creatures - bypass defensive blockers","Consistent clock - pressure before finisher turns online"]},recentSetImpact:{winterspell_february2026:{set:"Winterspell (Latest - Feb 13-20, 2026)",impact:"Winterspell cards are now integrated into established DLC lists, especially tempo and control shells.",keyCards:"Darkwing Duck - Dashing Gadgeteer, Launchpad - Trusty Sidekick, Winterspell are frequent inclusions.",advice:"Tune for efficient 2-4 cost interaction while preserving late-game card advantage."},whispers_november2025:{set:"Whispers in the Well (Nov 2025)",impact:"Boost mechanic enabled value/snowball strategies. Extended some game lengths.",innovation:"Boost-focused decks emerged but haven't dominated meta",advice:"Consider Boost mechanics in matchup analysis. Some decks snowball harder with Boost."},fabled_september2025:{set:"Fabled (Aug-Sep 2025)",impact:"Epic and Iconic rarities printed - highest power ceiling ever",keyCards:"Goofy Movie characters. Epic/Iconic cards from all inks.",advice:"If you haven't seen Fabled cards in meta yet, expect them to emerge in counters"},archazia_march2025:{set:"Archazia's Island (Mar 2025)",impact:"Dual-ink cards introduced - expanded deck flexibility",innovation:"Dual-ink cards not inherently more powerful, but enabled new builds",advice:"Dual-ink cards provide flexibility without breaking existing color balance"}},metaShiftWarnings:["Emerald/Sapphire remains the primary benchmark in current DLC fields","Winterspell-era Ruby/Steel tempo shells punish slow openings","Card-advantage mirrors are common - plan for longer games","Efficient interaction on turns 2-4 is increasingly important","Keep flexible slots for fast aggro and grindy control matchups"],flexSlotRecommendations:{against_currentMeta:["1x Cheap removal for Ruby Rush creatures (combat damage prevention)","1x Card draw engine piece (counter hand disruption from Amethyst)","1x Creature with Resist (defensive against aggro pressure)","1x Board wipe or mass answer (prevent snowballing)","1x Hand disruption piece (if not already in deck, pressure their setup)"],sideboard_if_available:["2-3 Resist creatures - transforms matchups vs Ruby/Amethyst","2x Early removal suite - flexes for aggro-heavy metagame","2x Card draw pieces - tech in vs hand disruption heavy meta","2x Evasive creatures - bypass defensive decks","2-3 Specific archetype counters - adjust to your local meta"]},tieringGuide:{tier_s:"Emerald/Sapphire Control - Most consistent top-table performer.",tier_1a:"Ruby/Steel Winterspell Tempo - High conversion in recent DLC events.",tier_1b:"Amethyst/Sapphire Value - Strong in midrange and control fields.",tier_2:"Amber/Emerald Dogs, Sapphire/Steel Control - Solid performers with favorable pairings",tier_3:"Rogue strategies, Mono-color decks - Can steal games but less consistent",advice:"Tier placement changes based on local metagame. Play what you understand."}},c={advancedConcepts:e,beginnerTips:a,intermediateTips:t,deckArchetypes:r,playstyleGuides:n,starterDeckAdvice:o,coachingTips:s,advancedCoachingStrategies:i,currentMeta:l};export{i as advancedCoachingStrategies,e as advancedConcepts,a as beginnerTips,s as coachingTips,l as currentMeta,r as deckArchetypes,c as default,t as intermediateTips,n as playstyleGuides,o as starterDeckAdvice};
